IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgba-nouns`
IMPORT `sgba-vintage`

-- INSTRUMENT: Broadcasting (Class Licence -- Broadcasting to Digital Display Panels) Notification 2020 (S 477/2020), made under s 9 of the Act.
-- Deposit: ../../../broadcasting-class-licence-digital-display-panels-notification-2020/registers/source-bundle/BA1994-S477-2020.txt (lawplain's rendering, line-broken by hand).
-- The class licence is for PROVIDERS of a licensable broadcasting service to display panels in public places or public passenger transport vehicles; it is not a licence
-- to own or use a television. Dated: the window of the Notification as deposited.

§ `Paragraph 2: Definitions`

-- src:7 | “class licensee” means a person to whom a class licence by virtue of this Notification applies but excludes a person for the time the application of that class licence is suspended or disapplied under the Act;
@ref para 2 "class licensee" (src:7)
GIVEN `a class licence by virtue of this Notification applies to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application of that class licence is suspended or disapplied under the Act for the time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 477/2020 para 2 the person is a class licensee` MEANS
    `a class licence by virtue of this Notification applies to the person` AND (NOT `the application of that class licence is suspended or disapplied under the Act for the time`)

-- src:8 | “digital display panel” means a screen, panel, computer monitor or similar appliance —
-- src:9 | ( a ) with minimum dimensions (excluding cables and connectors) of 17.78 centimetres when measured diagonally or at its widest; and
-- src:10 | ( b ) designed to be used primarily for the reception and display of any programme capable of being received, or received and displayed, as visual images (whether moving or still) with or without sound, from a licensable broadcasting service,
-- src:11 | and includes a screen, panel or similar appliance that has additional functions that are not required for its basic operation as described in paragraph ( b ) (such as interactive features) but excludes a mobile phone and a wearable device (like a smart watch);
@ref para 2 "digital display panel" (src:8-11)
GIVEN `it is a screen, panel, computer monitor or similar appliance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its minimum dimension, excluding cables and connectors, measured diagonally or at its widest, in centimetres` IS A NUMBER
      `it is designed to be used primarily for the reception and display of a programme from a licensable broadcasting service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a mobile phone or a wearable device` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 477/2020 para 2 the appliance is a digital display panel` MEANS
    `it is a screen, panel, computer monitor or similar appliance`
    AND `its minimum dimension, excluding cables and connectors, measured diagonally or at its widest, in centimetres` AT LEAST 17.78
    AND `it is designed to be used primarily for the reception and display of a programme from a licensable broadcasting service`
    AND (NOT `it is a mobile phone or a wearable device`)

-- src:12 | “HDB” means the Housing and Development Board established under the Housing and Development Act (Cap. 129);
@ref para 2 "HDB" (src:12)
GIVEN `it is the Housing and Development Board established under the Housing and Development Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 477/2020 para 2 the body is the HDB` MEANS
    `it is the Housing and Development Board established under the Housing and Development Act`

-- src:13 | “programme” includes any matter (whether or not advertising, sponsorship or otherwise), regardless that the matter may be exempt from classification under the Films Act (Cap. 107), but excludes the following matter:
-- src:14 | ( a ) matter that is broadcast on a free‑to‑air broadcasting service provided by a person holding a broadcasting licence granted under section 8 of the Act, but not a recording of the matter from that broadcast;
-- src:15 | ( b ) matter that is broadcast on a subscription nationwide television service (whether using cable or an Internet protocol) with scheduled programming, provided by a person holding a broadcasting licence granted under section 8 of the Act, but not a recording of the matter from that broadcast;
@ref para 2 "programme" (src:13-15)
GIVEN `it is matter, whether or not advertising, sponsorship or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is broadcast on a free-to-air broadcasting service provided by a person holding a broadcasting licence granted under section 8, and is not a recording of the matter from that broadcast` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is broadcast on a subscription nationwide television service with scheduled programming, provided by a person holding a broadcasting licence granted under section 8, and is not a recording of the matter from that broadcast` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 477/2020 para 2 the matter is a programme` MEANS
    `it is matter, whether or not advertising, sponsorship or otherwise` AND (NOT `it is broadcast on a free-to-air broadcasting service provided by a person holding a broadcasting licence granted under section 8, and is not a recording of the matter from that broadcast`) AND (NOT `it is broadcast on a subscription nationwide television service with scheduled programming, provided by a person holding a broadcasting licence granted under section 8, and is not a recording of the matter from that broadcast`)

-- src:16 | “public entertainment” has the meaning given by the Public Entertainments Act (Cap. 257);
@ref para 2 "public entertainment" (src:16)
-- Borrowed from the Public Entertainments Act: asked as a fact.
GIVEN `it is public entertainment within the meaning of the Public Entertainments Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 477/2020 para 2 the thing is public entertainment` MEANS
    `it is public entertainment within the meaning of the Public Entertainments Act`

-- src:17 | “public passenger transport vehicle” means —
-- src:18 | ( a ) a train used by a person to operate a rapid transit system as defined by the Rapid Transit Systems Act (Cap. 263A); or
-- src:19 | ( b ) a motor vehicle that is authorised for use as a public service vehicle by a licence issued under Part V of the Road Traffic Act (Cap. 276);
@ref para 2 "public passenger transport vehicle" (src:17-19)
GIVEN `it is a train used by a person to operate a rapid transit system as defined by the Rapid Transit Systems Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a motor vehicle authorised for use as a public service vehicle by a licence issued under Part V of the Road Traffic Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 477/2020 para 2 the vehicle is a public passenger transport vehicle` MEANS
    `it is a train used by a person to operate a rapid transit system as defined by the Rapid Transit Systems Act` OR `it is a motor vehicle authorised for use as a public service vehicle by a licence issued under Part V of the Road Traffic Act`

-- src:20 | “public place” means —
-- src:21 | ( a ) any place (open to the air or otherwise) to which members of the public have access as of right or by virtue of express or implied permission, without payment of a fee;
-- src:32 | ( b ) any place (open to the air or otherwise) to which members of the public have access on payment of a fee —
-- src:33 | (i) mainly for a purpose that is other than viewing a display or an exhibition of a film or programme for entertainment or in the course of education; and
-- src:34 | (ii) where viewing a display or an exhibition of a film or programme on a digital display panel is wholly incidental to the main purpose of entering the place; or
-- src:38 | ( c ) a public passenger transport vehicle on a journey within Singapore but not if the journey is between a place in Singapore and a place outside Singapore,
-- src:43 | regardless that access to the place or vehicle may be restricted at particular times, but excludes a cinema hall, movie theatre, mosque, temple, church or other place for public worship or for the conduct (temporary or otherwise) of religious ceremonies, rites, services or celebrations.
@ref para 2 "public place" (src:20-43)
GIVEN `it is a place to which members of the public have access as of right or by express or implied permission, without payment of a fee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a place to which members of the public have access on payment of a fee, mainly for a purpose other than viewing a display or exhibition of a film or programme for entertainment or in the course of education, and where viewing on a digital display panel is wholly incidental to that main purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a public passenger transport vehicle on a journey within Singapore, and the journey is not between a place in Singapore and a place outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a cinema hall, movie theatre, mosque, temple, church or other place for public worship or for the conduct of religious ceremonies, rites, services or celebrations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 477/2020 para 2 the place is a public place` MEANS
    (NOT `it is a cinema hall, movie theatre, mosque, temple, church or other place for public worship or for the conduct of religious ceremonies, rites, services or celebrations`)
    AND (`it is a place to which members of the public have access as of right or by express or implied permission, without payment of a fee` OR `it is a place to which members of the public have access on payment of a fee, mainly for a purpose other than viewing a display or exhibition of a film or programme for entertainment or in the course of education, and where viewing on a digital display panel is wholly incidental to that main purpose` OR `it is a public passenger transport vehicle on a journey within Singapore, and the journey is not between a place in Singapore and a place outside Singapore`)

§ `Paragraph 3: Class licence`

-- src:45 | 3. —(1) Unless exempt by or under section 60 of the Act or excluded by sub‑paragraph (2), every person who provides, in the course of business, any licensable broadcasting service in or from Singapore comprising transmission by signs or signals of any programme (with or without sound) for reception by and for display on —
-- src:46 | ( a ) 2 or more digital display panels each situated in a public place in Singapore; or
-- src:47 | ( b ) 2 or more digital display panels each installed within a public passenger transport vehicle,
-- src:48 | is subject to a class licence in connection with that broadcasting service.
@ref para 3(1) (src:45-48)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the person provides, in the course of business, a licensable broadcasting service in or from Singapore comprising transmission of a programme for reception by and for display on digital display panels` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of those panels each situated in a public place in Singapore` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those panels each installed within a public passenger transport vehicle` IS A NUMBER
      `the person is exempt by or under section 60 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is excluded by sub-paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`S 477/2020 para 3(1) the person is subject to a class licence in connection with the service, on` MEANS
    IF `the Digital Display Panels Notification as deposited is the text in force on` d
    THEN JUST (`the person provides, in the course of business, a licensable broadcasting service in or from Singapore comprising transmission of a programme for reception by and for display on digital display panels`
        AND (`the number of those panels each situated in a public place in Singapore` AT LEAST 2 OR `the number of those panels each installed within a public passenger transport vehicle` AT LEAST 2)
        AND (NOT `the person is exempt by or under section 60 of the Act`)
        AND (NOT `the person is excluded by sub-paragraph (2)`))
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:49 | (2) Sub-paragraph (1) does not apply to a person who provides, in the course of business, any licensable broadcasting service in or from Singapore any programme (with or without sound) solely for reception by and for display on a digital display panel (even if in a public place or public passenger transport vehicle) that is under the control (temporary or otherwise) or management of a person who —
-- src:50 | ( a ) is granted a licence under section 6 of the Films Act (Cap. 107) authorising the person to publicly exhibit any film in the course of business involving that digital display panel;
-- src:51 | ( b ) is subject to a class licence under the Films (Class Licence for Video Games Distribution) Order 2019 (G.N. No. S 342/2019) authorising the person to distribute and publicly exhibit any video game in the course of business involving that digital display panel;
-- src:52 | ( c ) is exempt from section 21(1) of the Films Act in respect of the public exhibition using that digital display panel of any exempt video game by reason of the Films (Classification — Exempt Video Games) Notification 2019 (G.N. No. S 339/2019); or
-- src:53 | ( d ) is the holder of a public entertainment licence granted under the Public Entertainments Act, or is exempt from that Act, in respect of the provision of public entertainment involving that digital display panel.
@ref para 3(2) (src:49-53)
GIVEN `the person provides the service solely for reception by and for display on a digital display panel under the control or management of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that person is granted a licence under section 6 of the Films Act to publicly exhibit films in the course of business involving the panel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that person is subject to the class licence under the Films (Class Licence for Video Games Distribution) Order 2019` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that person is exempt from section 21(1) of the Films Act in respect of public exhibition of an exempt video game using the panel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that person holds a public entertainment licence under the Public Entertainments Act, or is exempt from that Act, for public entertainment involving the panel` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 477/2020 para 3(2) sub-paragraph (1) does not apply to the person` MEANS
    `the person provides the service solely for reception by and for display on a digital display panel under the control or management of another person`
    AND (`that person is granted a licence under section 6 of the Films Act to publicly exhibit films in the course of business involving the panel`
         OR `that person is subject to the class licence under the Films (Class Licence for Video Games Distribution) Order 2019`
         OR `that person is exempt from section 21(1) of the Films Act in respect of public exhibition of an exempt video game using the panel`
         OR `that person holds a public entertainment licence under the Public Entertainments Act, or is exempt from that Act, for public entertainment involving the panel`)

§ `Paragraphs 4 and 5: Conditions`

-- src:55 | 4. A class licensee who provides a licensable broadcasting service described in paragraph 3(1) must not broadcast, or must discontinue the broadcast of, the whole or any part of a programme included in its service if the Authority informs the licensee that the whole or that part of the programme —
-- src:56 | ( a ) is contrary to a Code of Practice applicable to the licensee;
-- src:57 | ( b ) is against the public interest, public order or national harmony; or
-- src:58 | ( c ) offends against good taste or decency.
@ref para 4 (src:55-58)
GIVEN `the Authority has informed the licensee that the programme is contrary to a Code of Practice applicable to the licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority has informed the licensee that the programme is against the public interest, public order or national harmony` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority has informed the licensee that the programme offends against good taste or decency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 477/2020 para 4 the licensee must not broadcast, or must discontinue the broadcast of, the programme` MEANS
    `the Authority has informed the licensee that the programme is contrary to a Code of Practice applicable to the licensee`
    OR `the Authority has informed the licensee that the programme is against the public interest, public order or national harmony`
    OR `the Authority has informed the licensee that the programme offends against good taste or decency`

-- src:60 | 5. —(1) For the purpose of section 17 of the Act, a class licensee who provides a licensable broadcasting service described in paragraph 3(1) by transmitting, by signs or signals, any programme (with or without sound) for reception by and for display on any digital display panel situated on the wall of any lift landing, or in any lift, which is common property that —
-- src:61 | ( a ) is vested in or belonging to the HDB; and
-- src:62 | ( b ) relates to any building or premises used pursuant to the Planning Act (Cap. 232) wholly for the purpose of human habitation,
-- src:63 | must include in its licensable broadcasting service, on terms mentioned in sub‑paragraph (2), programmes provided by the Government through the Authority to the class licensee.
@ref para 5(1) (src:60-63)
GIVEN `the digital display panel is situated on the wall of a lift landing, or in a lift, which is common property vested in or belonging to the HDB` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it relates to a building or premises used pursuant to the Planning Act wholly for human habitation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 477/2020 para 5(1) the licensee must include in its service the programmes the Government provides through the Authority` MEANS
    `the digital display panel is situated on the wall of a lift landing, or in a lift, which is common property vested in or belonging to the HDB` AND `it relates to a building or premises used pursuant to the Planning Act wholly for human habitation`

-- src:64 | (2) The terms for the purposes of sub‑paragraph (1) are as follows:
-- src:65 | ( a ) no subsidy or compensation is payable to the class licensee for any programme provided to the class licensee by the Government through the Authority;
-- src:66 | ( b ) the display of programmes mentioned in sub‑paragraph ( a ) must make up 50% of the length of each content loop.
@ref para 5(2) (src:64-66)
GIVEN `the share of the length of each content loop, in per cent, that the Government's programmes make up` IS A NUMBER
      `a subsidy or compensation is payable to the licensee for them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 477/2020 para 5(2) the terms are met` MEANS
    (NOT `a subsidy or compensation is payable to the licensee for them`) AND `the share of the length of each content loop, in per cent, that the Government's programmes make up` AT LEAST 50

-- src:67 | (3) In determining whether sub‑paragraph (1) applies to a class licensee, the number of networks used by the class licensee is immaterial.
@ref para 5(3) (src:67)
GIVEN `the number of networks the licensee uses` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`S 477/2020 para 5(3) the number of networks used matters in deciding whether sub-paragraph (1) applies` MEANS
    FALSE

-- src:68 | (4) To avoid doubt, this paragraph applies in addition to paragraph 4 insofar as that paragraph concerns a class licensee described in sub‑paragraph (1).
@ref para 5(4) (src:68)
GIVEN `the licensee is described in sub-paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`S 477/2020 para 5(4) paragraph 5 applies in addition to paragraph 4` MEANS
    IF `the licensee is described in sub-paragraph (1)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
